    name: { de: "Chimaltenango", hu: "Chimaltenango", ro: "Chimaltenango", en: "Chimaltenango" },
    description: { de: "Hauptstadt des Departements Chimaltenango an der Panamericana.", hu: "Chimaltenango megye székhelye a Pánamerikai foútvonal mentén.", ro: "Capitala departamentului Chimaltenango, situata pe Autostrada Panamericana.", en: "Capital of the Chimaltenango department, located on the Pan-American Highway." },
    facts: { de: ["Hauptstadt von Chimaltenango", "An der Panamericana gelegen", "Landwirtschaftliche Region"], hu: ["Chimaltenango fovárosa", "A Pánamerikai foútvonalon található", "Mezogazdasági régió"], ro: ["Capitala Chimaltenango", "Situat pe Autostrada Panamericana", "Regiune agricola"], en: ["Capital of Chimaltenango", "On the Pan-American Highway", "Agricultural region"] },
    descriptionAdvanced: { de: "Chimaltenango liegt strategisch günstig an der Panamericana und ist die Hauptstadt des gleichnamigen Departements. Die Stadt fungiert als wichtiges landwirtschaftliches Verteilungszentrum für die fruchtbaren Ebenen der Umgebung. Hier werden große Mengen an Gemüse und Getreide produziert, die sowohl den nationalen Markt als auch den Export bedienen. Aufgrund ihrer Lage ist Chimaltenango ein geschäftiger Ort mit regem Handels- und Durchgangsverkehr. Die Stadt verbindet die Metropolregion im Osten mit dem westlichen Hochland von Guatemala.", hu: "Chimaltenango stratégiailag elonyös helyen, a Pánamerikai foútvonal mentén fekszik, és az azonos nevu megye székhelye. A város fontos mezogazdasági elosztó központként funkcionál a környezo termékeny síkságok számára. Itt nagy mennyiségben termelnek zöldséget és gabonát, amelyek mind a hazai piacot, mind az exportot kiszolgálják. Elhelyezkedése miatt Chimaltenango pezsgo hely, élénk kereskedelmi és tranzitforgalommal. A város összeköti a keleti metropolisz-régiót Guatemala nyugati felföldjével.", ro: "Situat pe o câmpie fertilă în apropierea lanțului vulcanic, Chimaltenango este renumit pentru agricultura sa bogată și piețele aglomerate. Istoric, a fost planificat de cuceritorii spanioli datorită climei sale favorabile, dar construcția a fost amânată după mutarea capitalei. Orașul este adesea considerat o poartă de acces majoră către zonele muntoase occidentale. Geografie K6 — topografia agricolă și economia locală.", en: "Located strategically along the Pan-American Highway, Chimaltenango serves as the capital of its namesake department and a major transit point connecting Guatemala City to the western highlands. Founded in 1526 by Pedro de Portocarrero, the city was historically known as 'B'oko'' before the Spanish arrived. Because it sits directly on the continental divide, water falling on the northern side of the city's central plaza flows towards the Atlantic, while water on the southern side flows to the Pacific. The local economy is driven by agriculture, particularly the large-scale production of vegetables, strawberries, and flowers for export, facilitated by the fertile volcanic soils. The city's unique position on the continental divide offers an excellent practical example for Geography K6 studies on watersheds." },
    factsAdvanced: { de: ["Chimaltenango ist die Hauptstadt des gleichnamigen Departements.", "Die Stadt liegt direkt an der wichtigen Fernstraße Panamericana.", "Die Region ist ein bedeutendes Zentrum für den Gemüseanbau in Guatemala.", "Sie bildet eine wichtige Brücke zwischen der Hauptstadt und dem Westen des Landes."], hu: ["Chimaltenango az azonos nevu megye székhelye.", "A város közvetlenül a fontos Pánamerikai foútvonal mentén fekszik.", "A régió a guatemalai zöldségtermesztés egyik kiemelkedo központja.", "Fontos hidat képez a fováros és az ország nyugati része között."], ro: ["Fondat de Pedro de Portocarrero în 1526.", "Faimos pentru fântâna colonială situată pe linia continentală de separație a apelor.", "Altitudinea de 1.800 de metri asigură un climat temperat.", "Exportator major de fructe, legume și textile tradiționale.", "Cutremurul devastator din 1976 a afectat grav structurile orașului.", "Orașul găzduiește o importantă biserică colonială."], en: ["Chimaltenango was founded in 1526 by Spanish conquistador Pedro de Portocarrero.", "The city sits exactly on the Americas' Continental Divide.", "It is positioned at an altitude of 1,800 meters above sea level.", "Before the Spanish conquest, the area was known by the Kaqchikel name 'B'oko'.", "The city's central fountain famously splits water towards two different oceans.", "It is a massive center for agricultural exports, including berries and textiles."] }
